Dear Jerome,

Thanks for your quick and helpful answer, which I post here to close this issue. As you mentioned in your answer, the "output" command should be set to "Wave" and not "matrix".  The script below worked perfect for me.

Thanks so much Jerome!!

Alle the best

Lutz

> > Ok, the issue comes from the 'rescale' argument that requires a Wave object, not a matrix (I will update it for the next version of seewave).
> > Try:
> >
> > # Filter the channel data - here with „rescale“ - without „rescale“ it works

> > VP01.a1 = ffilter(channel1, f=100, from = 0.07, to = 0.10, bandpass = TRUE,
> >                   custom = NULL, wl = wl, ovlp = ovlp, wn = "hanning", fftw = FALSE,

> >                   rescale=T, output="Wave")
> >
> > # rectify the filtered data
> > VP01.a1.abs = abs(VP01.a1@left)

